From a3ab652c7c82d10d56e9e8e96c6ae0a55d521bbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Mireles <davidmirelesll@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:57:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 07/21] fix(scripting): correct inverted vector component
 validation in jsToDynamicValue (#618)

ScriptEngine::jsToDynamicValue guards the JS->glm::vec conversion with:

    if (!JS_IsNumber (x) || JS_IsNumber (y)) {
        sLog.exception ("Vector's x and y components must be numbers");
    }

The second clause is missing a '!': a valid numeric y triggers the
exception (since sLog.exception is [[noreturn]] and throws runtime_error).
That breaks every JS->vec2/vec3/vec4 conversion from a scene script as
soon as the script passes a real vector literal.

Caught while auditing the scripting refactor in #599. Restore the
intended predicate so both x and y must be non-numeric to throw.

(cherry picked from commit 58a7f14ac18f3cdb67168702c5706b1dbe25fae9)

Origin: upstream-PR
Upstream-PR: https://github.com/Almamu/linux-wallpaperengine/pull/618
Adapted-by: livepaper
Why: a scene script passing a real vector to the engine threw on every JS->vec conversion
Status: upstream: merged on Almamu/linux-wallpaperengine main 2026-10-28, not (yet) on next-v2
---
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/Scripting/ScriptEngine.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Scripting/ScriptEngine.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Scripting/ScriptEngine.cpp
index 0af419c..6d9f4b7 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Scripting/ScriptEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Scripting/ScriptEngine.cpp
@@ -152,7 +152,7 @@ static void jsToDynamicValue (JSContext* ctx, JSValue val, DynamicValue& source)
 	    JS_FreeValue (ctx, w);
 	});
 
-	if (!JS_IsNumber (x) || JS_IsNumber (y)) {
+	if (!JS_IsNumber (x) || !JS_IsNumber (y)) {
 	    sLog.exception ("Vector's x and y components must be numbers");
 	}
 
